<title>IRAN: OPEC's Lukman calls for member output restraint.</title>
<headline>OPEC's Lukman calls for member output restraint.</headline>
<dateline>ISFAHAN, Iran 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC's Secretary-General Rilwanu Lukman on Friday called on OPEC producers to restrain their oil output to support prices ahead of the group's next meeting in Vienna in June.</p>
<p>&quot;The level of OPEC oil has to be restrained and the countries have agreed to try to do this over the next few weeks,&quot; he told reporters on the sidelines of an energy meeting in Isfahan.  </p>
<p>Lukman said that the production restraint was necessary so that oil prices did not fall below $18 a barrel.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still below the (OPEC's reference) price of $21...we do not want it (oil prices) to fall bellow $18 a barrel,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Independent estimates of OPEC production have put the organisation's output in April at over 27 million barrels per day in excess of the group's ceiling of 25.05 bpd.</p>
</text>
